Excluded Parties receive no permission under this License to use, operate, copy, reproduce, modify, adapt, merge, distribute, sublicense, sell, host, deploy, or incorporate the Software or a Modified Version.

This exclusion includes internal operations, research, product development, model training, fine-tuning, evaluation, benchmarking, and providing services. It applies to public and private activities that require permission from the applicable copyright holder.

No exception is provided for noncommercial use, internal use, research, testing, evaluation, attribution, or a short period of use.

An otherwise eligible user may not knowingly act as an intermediary to supply the Software, a Modified Version, or a dedicated deployment for an Excluded Party's organizational use.

Providing credit, preserving notices, paying another user, obtaining a copy through an intermediary, using a Modified Version, operating privately, or correcting a violation after discovery does not grant an Excluded Party permission under this License.

If an eligible user becomes an Excluded Party, permission ceases for activities covered by the exclusion from the time that status changes. Earlier permitted activities do not become violations solely because of that later change.

This exclusion is a mandatory limitation on permission, not a voluntary request. The correction period in Section 10 does not apply to it.

